Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:05:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] Add tab width bounds and tab chip settings

Tabs size to their title by default, which makes the tab bar uneven.
tabs.min_width and tabs.max_width clamp the tab width; editor and
terminal titles truncate in the middle when a maximum is set.

tab_bar.pinned_tab_chips and tab_bar.unpinned_tab_chips render the
tabs of the pinned or unpinned row as compact borderless chips that hug
their content. Chips are as tall as the toolbar's default buttons and
use the theme's element state colours.

The width bounds default to null and the chips to false, which keeps
the stock tab layout, including terminal titles in the tab switcher.
